    "name": "22.1 Protection of Individuals and Community",
    "text": "Section 22. Administrative Actions and Sanctions 22.1. Protection of Individuals and the Community: Whenever the University has reason to believe that a student’s conduct or behavior may pose a signicant threat to his or her physical or emotional safety or well-being, or may disrupt the safety or well-being of another student, faculty, staff, guest or other University community member, the University may take any action that it believes to be appropriate and reasonable under the circumstances. This may include but is not limited to, notication of the student’s parents, removal of the student from a residence hall, or other action deemed necessary to remove or minimize the threat or disruption."
