  {
    "id": "c109",
    "name": "22.4 Dean’s Sanctions",
    "text": "22.4. Dean’s Sanctions: Brandeis University expects students to conduct themselves at all times as good citizens and good neighbors in a manner that is consistent with the federal, state, and local laws and ordinances. Off-campus behavior which, in the judgment of the Dean of Student Life, constitutes behavior that is inconsistent with this expectation and adversely affects the University community may result in disciplinary action up to and including dismissal. A student disciplined under this authority may request a meeting with the Dean and the Student Conduct Board (SCB). The SCB shall advise the Dean on the appropriateness of the sanction. The nal decision shall be made by the Dean of Student Life or, in the Dean’s absence, by the Dean’s designee. The procedural standards set forth in Section 19 do not apply to off- campus behavior or Dean’s Sanction."
  },
  {
    "id": "c110",
    "name": "22.5 Medical and Emotional Emergencies",
    "text": "22.5. Medical and Emotional Emergencies: Whenever a student’s conduct results in the intervention of Brandeis’ Health Service, the Brandeis Psychological Counseling Center, or a non- Brandeis medical or psychological health care provider in order to prevent or address a student’s self-harm or harm to others, or to address a student’s severe emotional or psychological distress, the Dean of Student Life will establish an emergency protocol for that student. Any student who receives treatment from a non-Brandeis medical or psychological health care provider under these circumstances must contact the Dean upon release."
  },
  {
    "id": "c111",
    "name": "22.5 Emergency Protocol Notice and Review",
    "text": "The Dean shall notify the student in writing of the emergency protocol and the basis for the protocol. Within three class days of notication, the student shall have an opportunity to speak with the Dean, or the Dean’s designee, to discuss the protocol and provide information, including documentation by a health care provider, to contest the action(s) taken. The Dean shall then decide, at the Dean’s discretion, whether to reinstate or restore the student’s privileges, to consider further action under this procedure, or to take additional reasonable and appropriate steps."
  },
  {
    "id": "c112",
    "name": "22.5 Emergency Protocol Restrictions",
    "text": "During the period begun by the emergency intervention and continuing until the conveyance of explicit written permission by the Dean of Student Life (or designee) to resume campus functions, a student subject to an emergency protocol is not permitted to access any campus property, facilities or attend any classes. There will be no exception for examinations or other time-sensitive student activities or academic obligations. Failure to comply with this protocol may result in referral to the Student Conduct Process as dened in this document."
  },
  {
    "id": "c113",
    "name": "23 Hearing Participants",
    "text": "Section 23. Hearing Procedures for the Student Conduct Process1 All hearing participants are brought into the Board meeting room."
  },
  {
    "id": "c114",
    "name": "23.A Introductions",
    "text": "A. Chairperson invites all present to introduce themselves."
  },
  {
    "id": "c115",
    "name": "23.B Explanation of Procedures",
    "text": "B. Chairperson explains philosophy of peer judgment and Board procedures (a copy of this statement is available from the Department of Student Rights and Community Standards)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c116",
    "name": "23.C Statement of Rights",
    "text": "C. Chairperson gives statement of the student’s rights to fairness under this process: 1. To bring one adviser of the accused/accuser’s choice from the University community to provide passive assistance during the hearing (the adviser may not serve as a witness) 2. To present witnesses on their own behalf 3. To question witnesses appearing against them 4. To submit verbal arguments 5. To remain silent and not testify against themselves. The accused/accuser should remember that if they remain silent, the Board is compelled to hear the case and render a decision based upon the evidence presented."
  },
  {
    "id": "c117",
    "name": "23.D Witnesses Leave",
    "text": "D. Witnesses leave the room"
  },
  {
    "id": "c118",
    "name": "23.E Statement of Accusations",
    "text": "E. Chairperson gives statement of accusations"
  },
  {
    "id": "c119",
    "name": "23.E.1 Understanding Accusations",
    "text": "1. The accused is asked if sh/e understands the accusations"
  },
  {
    "id": "c120",
    "name": "23.E.2 Responsibility Plea",
    "text": "2. The accused accepts or denies responsibility"
  },
  {
    "id": "c121",
    "name": "23.F Multiple Accused Presentations",
    "text": "F. Initial presentations: In the event that there is more than one accused, the Board may bring them into the hearing room either individually or as a group for descriptions of the incident in alphabetical order; this system shall prevail throughout the remainder of the hearing procedures."
  },
  {
    "id": "c122",
    "name": "23.F.1 Accuser Presentation",
    "text": "1. The accuser offers their description of incident"
  },
  {
    "id": "c123",
    "name": "23.F.2 Accused Presentation",
    "text": "2. The accused offers their description of the incident"
  },
  {
    "id": "c124",
    "name": "23.F.3 Accused Questions Accuser",
    "text": "3. The accused may ask questions of the accuser"
  },
  {
    "id": "c125",
    "name": "23.F.4 Board Questions Accuser",
    "text": "4. Board members may ask questions of the accuser"
  },
  {
    "id": "c126",
    "name": "23.F.5 Accuser Questions Accused",
    "text": "5. The accuser may ask questions of the accused"
  },
  {
    "id": "c127",
    "name": "23.F.6 Board Questions Accused",

    "name": "23.F.6 Board Questions Accused",
    "text": "6. Board members may ask questions of the accused"
  },
  {
    "id": "c128",
    "name": "23.G Accuser Witnesses",
    "text": "G. Witnesses for the accuser may be called"
  },
  {
    "id": "c129",
    "name": "23.G.1 Accuser Questions Witness",
    "text": "1. The accuser may ask questions of the witness"
  },
  {
    "id": "c130",
    "name": "23.G.2 Accused Questions Witness",
    "text": "2. The accused may ask questions of the witness"
  },
  {
    "id": "c131",
    "name": "23.G.3 Board Questions Witness",
    "text": "3. Board members may ask questions of the witness"
  },
  {
    "id": "c132",
    "name": "23.G.4 Witness Excused",
    "text": "4. Witness is excused from the hearing room (but retained outside for possible recall)"
  },
  {
    "id": "c133",
    "name": "23.H Accused Witnesses",
    "text": "H. Witnesses for the accused may be called"
  },
  {
    "id": "c134",
    "name": "23.H.1 Accused Questions Witness",
    "text": "1. The accused may ask questions of the witness"
  },
  {
    "id": "c135",
    "name": "23.H.2 Accuser Questions Witness",
    "text": "2. The accuser may ask questions of the witness"
  },
  {
    "id": "c136",
    "name": "23.H.3 Board Questions Witness",
    "text": "3. Board members may ask questions of the witness"
  },
  {
    "id": "c137",
    "name": "23.H.4 Witness Excused",
    "text": "4. Witness is excused from the hearing room (but retained outside for possible recall through Step M.)"
  },
  {
    "id": "c138",
    "name": "23 Hearing Procedure Variations",
    "text": "1 Hearing procedures may differ in cases involving allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual harassment or sex discrimination in accordance with Title IX."
  },
  {
    "id": "c139",
    "name": "23.I Recall of Witnesses",
    "text": "I. The accuser, the accused, or Board members may recall witnesses or re-question the accuser or accused (following same order as previous witness questioning)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c140",
    "name": "23.J Accuser Final Statement",
    "text": "J. Final statement of accuser (no new testimony)"
  },
  {
    "id": "c141",
    "name": "23.K Accused Final Statement",
    "text": "K. Final statement of accused (no new testimony)"
  },
  {
    "id": "c142",
    "name": "23.L Participants Leave Hearing Room",
    "text": "L. Accuser, accused, and their respective advisers leave hearing room, but remain outside."
  },
  {
    "id": "c143",
    "name": "23.M Board Deliberation",
    "text": "M. Board deliberates on responsibility"
  },
  {
    "id": "c144",
    "name": "23.M Decision Announcement",
    "text": "After the board reaches a determination any remaining witnesses in the waiting area are excused. The accused, the accuser, and advisers are called back into the hearing room to hear the decision on responsibility."
  },
  {
    "id": "c145",
    "name": "23.N Not Responsible Outcome",
    "text": "N. If the accused is found not responsible for all charges, all are excused and hearing is adjourned. An outcome notication (via Brandeis e-mail) will be sent to the accused, usually within 3-5 business days."
  },
  {
    "id": "c146",
    "name": "23.O Sanction Recommendations",
    "text": "O. If the accused is found responsible for one or more charges, recommendations and questions on sanction(s) are heard."
  },
  {
    "id": "c147",
    "name": "23.O.1 Accuser Sanction Recommendation",
    "text": "1. The Board hears recommendations from the accuser regarding a possible sanction(s)"
  },
  {
    "id": "c148",
    "name": "23.O.1.a Accused Response",
    "text": "a. The accused may question the accuser and/or make a statement regarding recommended sanction(s)"
  },
  {
    "id": "c149",
    "name": "23.O.1.b Accuser Questions Accused",
    "text": "b. The accuser may question the accused on the recommended sanction(s)"
  },
  {
    "id": "c150",
    "name": "23.O.1.c Board Questions Parties",
    "text": "c. The Board may question the accused and the accuser on the recommended sanction(s)"
  },
  {
    "id": "c151",
    "name": "23.O.2 Sanction Deliberation Notice",
    "text": "2. The accuser, the accused and their respective advisers are informed that the Board will deliberate on sanction recommendations which will be communicated to the Director of Student Rights and Community Standards, Associate Dean of Student Life and/or Dean of Student Life. Final sanction determinations will be communicated in writing to the accused, and in some cases to the accuser, usually within 3-5 business days. The accused, the accuser, and advisers are excused and the Board reserves the right to adjourn for later deliberations."
  },
  {
    "id": "c152",
    "name": "23.P Sanction Deliberations",
    "text": "P. The Board deliberates on sanction recommendations."
  },
  {
    "id": "c153",
    "name": "23.P.1 Past Conduct Information",
    "text": "1. The Board is advised of past conduct involvement of the accused, if any, by the Hearing Administrator."
  },
  {
    "id": "c154",
    "name": "23.P.2 Recording Recommendations",
    "text": "2. The Hearing Administrator will record the Board’s recommendations, which will be reviewed by the appropriate administrator."
  },
  {
    "id": "c155",
    "name": "23 Appeal Procedures Notice",
    "text": "Appeal procedures will be addressed in the nal outcome letter to the accused and, in some cases, the accuser."
  }
]
